-- WITHIN d OF THE DEADLINE names the ENCLOSING obligation's deadline
-- (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.1, R-Q7B). Here the enclosing obligation
-- has no WITHIN at all — not on its act, and (it is not an EVERY) not on a
-- join line — so there is no deadline to name.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer
    Seller

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay
    Deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST Pay
    HENCE (PARTY Seller MUST Deliver WITHIN 5 OF THE DEADLINE)
